  "dispositions": {
    "Enabled Relations.Contains": "R1990 and R1991 govern obsolete Enabled Relations.Contains property paths, while Current R2511 and R2464 separately declare Plan and Workflow containment. Their unique prose details need claim-by-claim integration; do not silently retire or map the missing property to an instance field.",
    "Governance Origin": "R1645 and R1690 both actively govern Atom.Governance Origin and impose distinct origin/obligation rules; no currently verified Property Declaration establishes this subject. Do not invent a Header property or remove rules.",
    "History": "R1644 actively governs Journal; History is merely a passive model-node reference while preserved history remains ordinary evidence in its Claim. Preview removes only the undeclared passive path, preserving all Claim, Summary and other metadata."
  },
  "unresolved_question": "Should Governance Origin remain a declared Atom Property, or should its existing internal/external ownership rules instead govern another already-declared subject?",
  "limits": "No native source/Draft, code, test, Workflow, Workbench or Git change. A preview does not close the audit flag or authorize retirement.",
